      "prompt_tokens": 18,
      "completion_tokens": 1190,
      "output": "Water is a chemical substance that is essential for life on Earth. Here is a breakdown of what it is, how it is made, and why it is unique:\n\n### 1. Chemical Composition\nChemically, water is known as **dihydrogen monoxide**. Its chemical formula is **$H_2O$**. This means that every molecule of water is made up of:\n*   **Two hydrogen atoms**\n*   **One oxygen atom**\n\nThese atoms are bonded together by a covalent bond.\n\n### 2. The States of Matter\nWhile we usually think of water as a liquid, it exists in all three states of matter:\n*   **Solid:** When frozen, it becomes ice.\n*   **Liquid:** This is the state we see in oceans, rivers, and rain.\n*   **Gas:** When heated, it turns into steam or water vapor.\n\n### 3. Unique Properties\nWater is not just a random liquid; it has several properties that make it unique in the universe:\n*   **Polarity:** The oxygen atom pulls electrons away from the hydrogen atoms, giving the molecule a \"V\" shape. This makes one end of the molecule slightly positive and the other slightly negative. This allows water molecules to stick together (cohesion) and to other substances (adhesion).\n*   **The Universal Solvent:** Because of its polarity, water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This is why it is the main transport system in the human body and in nature.\n*   **High Surface Tension:** Water molecules stick together very strongly at the surface, creating a kind of \"skin.\" This allows small insects to walk on water.\n*   **High Specific Heat Capacity:** Water can absorb a lot of heat before it gets hot, and it releases a lot of heat before it freezes. This helps regulate the Earth's climate and keeps our bodies at a stable temperature.\n\n### 4. Biological Importance\nWater is the foundation of life. It is required for:\n*   **Digestion:** Breaking down food.\n*   **Transport:** Moving nutrients and oxygen to cells.\n*   **Temperature Regulation:** Sweating and panting to cool down.\n*   **Cellular Function:** All chemical reactions inside our cells happen in water."
